{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4c1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae85-6f28-7820-bd16-47b81c37dfdf"},"sequence":187,"recorded_at":1780531400000369,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b4a1c3d7-49d0-4a3e-844c-4f8e7f124ef3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b4a1c3d7-49d0-4a3e-844c-4f8e7f124ef3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b4a1c3d7-49d0-4a3e-844c-4f8e7f124ef3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae85-ed2e-7213-8219-9f7585342f0a"},"task_id":"01a0ae85-ed2e-7213-8219-9f7585342f0a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae85-ed2e-7213-8219-9f7585342f0a","chunk":"Read text file `LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-17\n7|\n8|### TASK-260830-2zvo8m — native-resume smoke framework (story-final leaf)\n9|\n10|- PRODUCTION: new `internal/resumesmoke` (`Run` drives probe,\n11|  identify-session, discovery-bind, quiescence-precondition, and\n12|  resume-plan through `provhost.Host.Call`; `ResumeCell` reads the\n13|  Section 8.4 native-resume direction with Appendix B version gates;\n14|  `VerifyRecord` enforces the closed smoke record, omit-self digest,\n15|  and verdict consistency; `Store`/`Load` install content-addressed,\n16|  no-replace, fsynced evidence) plus two zero-refusal-site provhost\n17|  replay accessors (`ProbeBuild`, `SplitIdentifyResult`) that consume\n18|  validated members, never the body.\n19|- REFUSAL DIRECTION: U/? tuples refuse before any adapter call; C\n20|  tuples gather read-only evidence and gate the resume plan with the\n21|  Section 19.3 citation; only A cells pass. No smoke API promotes a\n22|  gated cell, and passing smoke advertises no capability (no\n23|  capability map, no doctor surface; Section 8.3 stays the only\n24|  authority). Muse off-pin reads unknown (Appendix B unsettled),\n25|  matching the landed tuple gate.\n26|- MUTANTS: committed `TestSmokeMutantsAreKilled` kills 10/10\n27|  narrowing mutants (resume gate, probe drift, confidence, bind,\n28|  digest scope, consistency, disagreement length, quiescence,\n29|  mapping, matrix) with the harmless comment control SURVIVED. Each\n30|  mutant runs in a private module copy: the first harness patched\n31|  the checkout in place and raced parallel tree-walking censuses\n32|  (`specdoc` read a half-written file under `go test ./...`), so\n33|  the shipped harness never writes the checkout.\n34|- DEFECTS FOUND BY TESTS (fixed): record verification carried two\n35|  equivalent integrity checks (canonical reconstruction subsumed the\n36|  omit-self digest compare, which could never fire independently) -\n37|  dropped reconstruction, kept the owner-idiom digest compare; crash\n38|  test scanned a 19-char prefix of a 20-char filename and missed the\n39|  killed install.\n40|- IDEMPOTENCY/CRASH: identical inputs replay byte-identical records;\n41|  identical Store retries reuse the path; disagreeing bytes refuse\n42|  for quarantine; real-kill test (`SIGKILL` between write and fsync\n43|  via re-executed helper) recovers byte-identical evidence.\n44|- TRACEABILITY (story-close): bindings for 2.4 (full 4/4), 5.5\n45|  (sliver 1/3), 7.7 (partial 3/4), 8 (sliver 4/12) with 12 new\n46|  acceptance cases; `tracecheck` now 113 cases, 29/463 clauses;\n47|  `-section 2.4` admitted alongside 6.2; README figures and pin\n48|  tests updated deliberately.\n49|- BOUNDS (stated): native-Windows bind rows need a Windows host\n50|  (host separator vs platform-native proof rule) and skip loudly on\n51|  POSIX with cells still pinned by derivation; quiescence consumed\n52|  as valid-and-safe only (proof-to-tuple binding belongs to the\n53|  quiescence owner); record integrity detects tampering, not a\n54|  digest-plus-checklist forgery (local evidence, no adversary).\n55|- COVERAGE: 16 of 16 AC rows driven through production entries;\n56|  results, conformance matrix, and producer evidence tarball\n57|  attached to the task; candidate left uncommitted.\n58|\n59|### TASK-260830-3uzfyn — profile resolution, set-profile, and provider mapping\n60|- PRODUCTION: new `internal/sessprofile` (Section 2.4 derivation over\n61|  the session head and the checkpoint event-head closure, `Projector`\n62|  over the sessrepo entries, pure `MintChangeEvent`, `Transactor`\n63|  set-profile with replay-on-retry, reducer-level pair\n64|  projections/checks, `ResolveCreationProfile`) plus provhost\n65|  `ResolveMapping`/`ProjectLaunchArgv` and the seventh refusal\n66|  constructor `failMappingUnavailable` (Section 2.4 code, exit 6).\n67|  Sections 2.4/7.7 are textually identical in v0.5.0/v0.6.0.\n68|- GATES: 12 new derived refusal arms (10 `invalid_config`, 2\n69|  `profile_mapping_unavailable`), all witnessed (floor 217 -> 229);\n70|  runtime audit extended to the seventh constructor and the closed\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
