{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4c7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae85-6f28-7820-bd16-47b81c37dfdf"},"sequence":190,"recorded_at":1780531400000375,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b4a1c3d7-49d0-4a3e-844c-4f8e7f124ef3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b4a1c3d7-49d0-4a3e-844c-4f8e7f124ef3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b4a1c3d7-49d0-4a3e-844c-4f8e7f124ef3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae85-ed87-7c72-9f0d-7171474c3d1a"},"task_id":"01a0ae85-ed87-7c72-9f0d-7171474c3d1a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae85-ed87-7c72-9f0d-7171474c3d1a","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-6-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git show HEAD:LOGBOOK.md | sed -n '1,20p'; echo ===CURRENT-README-REGEN===; grep -n \\\"Regenerate and verify\\\" README.md; sed -n '2745,2770p' README.md; echo ===HEAD-README-REGEN===; git show HEAD:README.md | grep -n \\\"Regenerate and verify\\\"; git show HEAD:README.md | sed -n '/Regenerate and verify/,/Specification-to-Code/p' | head -30\",\n  \"description\": \"Compare README regenerate blocks\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260917-3lt2xv — release-agnostic cataloggen check via -adopted\\n- CONTRACT: validation command 21 was pinned to explicit v0.6.0 inputs, so a Story re-pointing the catalog at a new revision failed construction at its own gate. The fix declares the adopted release once (`catalog.Adopted`, consumed by `Current()`) and adds a cataloggen `-adopted` mode deriving `internal/catalog/catalog.<adopted>.json` and `internal/specpin/<adopted>.lock.json` relative to `-root` (default \\\".\\\"). Mixed `-adopted` with explicit `-metadata`/`-contracts`, a missing derived input (message names the derived path), and a lock whose source release differs from adopted are refused before generation; otherwise the same Generate call and `-check`/`-output` semantics run byte-identically to the explicit form.\\n- GATE: command 21 is now `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check`; every other validation command unchanged. No catalog content, metadata, lock, or generated-output change.\\n- TESTS: adopted positives, byte-identity (adopted vs explicit v0.6.0 vs committed), and all refusals driven through the production `run` entry; the configured-command test asserts the `-adopted` shape and runs it rooted at the repo. Narrowing mutants per refusal plus a byte-identity derivation mutant, all killed; harmless control SURVIVED. Both the candidate `-adopted` command and trunk's explicit command are green on the tree.\\n- DOCS: README regenerate block and tool row document the `-adopted` form and the explicit equivalent. No behavior or availability claims added.\\n### TASK-260830-3uzfyn — profile resolution, set-profile, and provider mapping\\n- PRODUCTION: new `internal/sessprofile` (Section 2.4 derivation over\\n  the session head and the checkpoint event-head closure, `Projector`\\n  over the sessrepo entries, pure `MintChangeEvent`, `Transactor`\\n  set-profile with replay-on-retry, reducer-level pair\\n  projections/checks, `ResolveCreationProfile`) plus provhost\\n  `ResolveMapping`/`ProjectLaunchArgv` and the seventh refusal\\n  constructor `failMappingUnavailable` (Section 2.4 code, exit 6).\\n===CURRENT-README-REGEN===\\n2751:Regenerate and verify the committed output with:\\ntheir reviewed idempotency scope and crash/lost-result recovery evidence;\\nTerminal Backend entries reproduce the distinct Section 4.C canonical keys.\\nCapability entries are vocabulary members only: the public type has no\\navailability, enabled, supported, or status field, so catalog generation cannot\\nadvertise runtime capability.\\n\\nRegenerate and verify the committed output with:\\n\\n```bash\\ngo generate ./internal/catalog\\ngo run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\\ngo test ./internal/catalog ./internal/cataloggen ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -count=1\\n```\\n\\n## Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate\\n\\n[`internal/traceability`](internal/traceability) provides the read-only\\nrepository gate used by CI. Its reviewed\\n[`ownership.v0.6.0.json`](internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json)\\nregistry independently enumerates implementation owners for all 63 current\\ncontract rows, 36 pinned or catalog-referenced normative section keys, 113\\nexecutable acceptance cases, 56 exact section bindings with their declared\\ncoverage, 12 disclosed unowned sections, and 32 exact fixture identities or\\nAppendix D anchors. The v0.4.3 projection is checked as an owned 55-contract subset,\\nand the superseded v0.5.0 registry is checked as an owned legacy projection.\\nThe generated v0.6.0 catalog also carries the reviewed schema/version/self-field\\n===HEAD-README-REGEN===\\n2694:Regenerate and verify the committed output with:\\nRegenerate and verify the committed output with:\\n\\n```bash\\ngo generate ./internal/catalog\\ngo run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\\ngo test ./internal/catalog ./internal/cataloggen ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -count=1\\n```\\n\\nThe `-adopted` form derives the metadata and lock inputs from the code-level\\nadopted release, so the check stays valid when the adopted release changes.\\nThe explicit equivalent pins the same inputs by path:\\n\\n```bash\\ngo run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\\n```\\n\\n## Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4628,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1157,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4c9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae85-6f28-7820-bd16-47b81c37dfdf"},"sequence":191,"recorded_at":1780531400000377,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b4a1c3d7-49d0-4a3e-844c-4f8e7f124ef3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b4a1c3d7-49d0-4a3e-844c-4f8e7f124ef3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b4a1c3d7-49d0-4a3e-844c-4f8e7f124ef3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae85-ed87-7c72-9f0d-7171474c3d1a"},"task_id":"01a0ae85-ed87-7c72-9f0d-7171474c3d1a","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0ae85-ed87-7c72-9f0d-7171474c3d1a"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4cb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae85-6f28-7820-bd16-47b81c37dfdf"},"sequence":192,"recorded_at":1780531400000379,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b4a1c3d7-49d0-4a3e-844c-4f8e7f124ef3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"b4a1c3d7-49d0-4a3e-844c-4f8e7f124ef3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b4a1c3d7-49d0-4a3e-844c-4f8e7f124ef3"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae85e2a47736a845f6a7052f2d13","text":"Read text file `LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-17\n7|\n8|### TASK-260830-2zvo8m — native-resume smoke framework (story-final leaf)\n9|\n10|- PRODUCTION: new `internal/resumesmoke` (`Run` drives probe,\n11|  identify-session, discovery-bind, quiescence-precondition, and\n12|  resume-plan through `provhost.Host.Call`; `ResumeCell` reads the\n13|  Section 8.4 native-resume direction with Appendix B version gates;\n14|  `VerifyRecord` enforces the closed smoke record, omit-self digest,\n15|  and verdict consistency; `Store`/`Load` install content-addressed,\n16|  no-replace, fsynced evidence) plus two zero-refusal-site provhost\n17|  replay accessors (`ProbeBuild`, `SplitIdentifyResult`) that consume\n18|  validated members, never the body.\n19|- REFUSAL DIRECTION: U/? tuples refuse before any adapter call; C\n20|  tuples gather read-only evidence and gate the resume plan with the\n21|  Section 19.3 citation; only A cells pass. No smoke API promotes a\n22|  gated cell, and passing smoke advertises no capability (no\n23|  capability map, no doctor surface; Section 8.3 stays the only\n24|  authority). Muse off-pin reads unknown (Appendix B unsettled),\n25|  matching the landed tuple gate.\n26|- MUTANTS: committed `TestSmokeMutantsAreKilled` kills 10/10\n27|  narrowing mutants (resume gate, probe drift, confidence, bind,\n28|  digest scope, consistency, disagreement length, quiescence,\n29|  mapping, matrix) with the harmless comment control SURVIVED. Each\n30|  mutant runs in a private module copy: the first harness patched\n31|  the checkout in place and raced parallel tree-walking censuses\n32|  (`specdoc` read a half-written file under `go test ./...`), so\n33|  the shipped harness never writes the checkout.\n34|- DEFECTS FOUND BY TESTS (fixed): record verification carried two\n35|  equivalent integrity checks (canonical reconstruction subsumed the\n36|  omit-self digest compare, which could never fire independently) -\n37|  dropped reconstruction, kept the owner-idiom digest compare; crash\n38|  test scanned a 19-char prefix of a 20-char filename and missed the\n39|  killed install.\n40|- IDEMPOTENCY/CRASH: identical inputs replay byte-identical records;\n41|  identical Store retries reuse the path; disagreeing bytes refuse\n42|  for quarantine; real-kill test (`SIGKILL` between write and fsync\n43|  via re-executed helper) recovers byte-identical evidence.\n44|- TRACEABILITY (story-close): bindings for 2.4 (full 4/4), 5.5\n45|  (sliver 1/3), 7.7 (partial 3/4), 8 (sliver 4/12) with 12 new\n46|  acceptance cases; `tracecheck` now 113 cases, 29/463 clauses;\n47|  `-section 2.4` admitted alongside 6.2; README figures and pin\n48|  tests updated deliberately.\n49|- BOUNDS (stated): native-Windows bind rows need a Windows host\n50|  (host separator vs platform-native proof rule) and skip loudly on\n51|  POSIX with cells still pinned by derivation; quiescence consumed\n52|  as valid-and-safe only (proof-to-tuple binding belongs to the\n53|  quiescence owner); record integrity detects tampering, not a\n54|  digest-plus-checklist forgery (local evidence, no adversary).\n55|- COVERAGE: 16 of 16 AC rows driven through production entries;\n56|  results, conformance matrix, and producer evidence tarball\n57|  attached to the task; candidate left uncommitted.\n58|\n59|### TASK-260830-3uzfyn — profile resolution, set-profile, and provider mapping\n60|- PRODUCTION: new `internal/sessprofile` (Section 2.4 derivation over\n61|  the session head and the checkpoint event-head closure, `Projector`\n62|  over the sessrepo entries, pure `MintChangeEvent`, `Transactor`\n63|  set-profile with replay-on-retry, reducer-level pair\n64|  projections/checks, `ResolveCreationProfile`) plus provhost\n65|  `ResolveMapping`/`ProjectLaunchArgv` and the seventh refusal\n66|  constructor `failMappingUnavailable` (Section 2.4 code, exit 6).\n67|  Sections 2.4/7.7 are textually identical in v0.5.0/v0.6.0.\n68|- GATES: 12 new derived refusal arms (10 `invalid_config`, 2\n69|  `profile_mapping_unavailable`), all witnessed (floor 217 -> 229);\n70|  runtime audit extended to the seventh constructor and the closed\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
